WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
When someone is choking and can't breathe, cough, or make a sound, you have to move quickly.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
First, always check for consent. Ask them clearly,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Are you choking? Can I help you?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
If they nod yes, you're going to alternate between two main moves,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
five back blows and five abdominal thrusts.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.000
To perform back blows, stand behind them, lean them forward so gravity helps you out,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
and use the heel of your hand to give five firm, separate hits right between their shoulder blades.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
For abdominal thrusts, if the object is still there, wrap your arms around their waist.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Make a fist, place the thumb side just above their belly button,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.000
and grab that fist with your other hand.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Give five quick, sharp pulls inward and upward.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Keep switching between those five blows and five thrusts until the object pops out or the person passes out.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.000
If they do pass out and they lose consciousness, lower them gently to the floor.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Call 911 immediately and start CPR.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Quick tip, if the person is pregnant or too large for you to reach around their waist,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.000
do those thrusts on the center of their chest instead.

